    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is defined by the high-upside matchup for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.30), who remains our top play. Despite the platoon disadvantage against a left-hander, he benefits from a favorable matchup against Abbott and a significant boost from his leadoff spot, making him the anchor for our stolen base production. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) and **Yordan Alvarez** (61.80) follow closely behind; **Schmitt** is surging thanks to a positive platoon split against the right-handed Lorenzen, while **Alvarez** maintains elite status despite the L/L matchup because his xwOBA profile is simply too strong to ignore. Similarly, **Kazuma Okamoto** (61.78) provides high value today, capitalizing on a weak 5.58 xERA from M\u00e1rquez to maximize his run-production potential in the heart of the order.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (40.59), who hovered just above our 40-point floor but was ultimately relegated to the bench in favor of more efficient platoon alignments elsewhere. His proximity to the start threshold makes him the clear primary utility backup should a late-day scratch occur. We are proceeding with caution regarding our top-tier hitters facing elite arms; **Trea Turner** (55.76), **Kyle Schwarber** (54.35), and **Christian Yelich** (53.19) all face significant resistance against Skubal and Skenes. While their base projections remain steady, their efficiency scores are hampered by SP skill headwinds. We will monitor these specific matchups closely, as any deviation in the expected pitch usage could see their sub-60 scores fluctuate as we manage our daily game caps.",
